Top-level `validation` is not part of `ObjectFormSchema`. Validation is specified per field via `FormField.validation` (see `packages/types/src/form.ts`). Please update this example accordingly.
```suggestion
  "customFields": [
    {
      "name": "email",
      "type": "email",
      "label": "Email",
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "name": "password",
      "type": "password",
      "label": "Password",
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "name": "confirm_password",
      "type": "password",
      "label": "Confirm Password",
      "required": true,
      "validation": {
        "match": "password",
        "message": "Passwords must match"
      }
    }
  ]
```

`ObjectFormSchema.onSuccess` is a callback function that `ObjectForm` calls directly (`await schema.onSuccess(...)`). Providing an action object here (`{ type: 'toast', ... }`) will throw at runtime. Update the snippet to show a function callback for React usage.
```suggestion
        onSuccess: () => {
          // e.g. trigger a toast or any other side-effect here
          console.log('User created!');
        }
```

`ObjectFormSchema.onSuccess` is a callback function and is invoked directly by `ObjectForm` (`await schema.onSuccess(...)`). Setting it to an action object here will throw at runtime. Update this snippet to show a function callback (and note that callbacks are not JSON-serializable).
```suggestion
  onSuccess: async (result) => {
    // Note: callbacks are not JSON-serializable and must be defined in code, not in JSON.
    alert('Contact created!');
```

This example uses `columns: [{ field: ... }]`, but `TableColumn` uses `accessorKey` (not `field`), and keys like `format`/`badge` aren’t part of `TableColumn` (see `packages/types/src/data-display.ts`). Update the example to the actual `TableColumn` shape.
```suggestion
      "accessorKey": "name",
      "header": "Product Name"
    },
    {
      "accessorKey": "price",
      "header": "Price"
    },
    {
      "accessorKey": "status",
      "header": "Status"
```

For select fields, `FormField.options` is `SelectOption[]` with `{ label, value }` (see `packages/types/src/form.ts`). Using `options: ["Admin", "User", ...]` here doesn’t match the expected shape and is unlikely to render correctly.
```suggestion
        options: [
          { label: "Admin", value: "admin" },
          { label: "User", value: "user" },
          { label: "Guest", value: "guest" }
        ],
        required: true
      },
      { 
        name: "status", 
        label: "Status", 
        type: "select",
        options: [
          { label: "Active", value: "active" },
          { label: "Inactive", value: "inactive" }
        ],
```
